===========================================================================
PARITY NOTES (web TripLegList.tsx -> native; web is THE spec)
===========================================================================
  • Empty (web `legItems.length === 0`)  -> .empty phase: title "Route Breakdown" + a friendly
    "Plan a trip to see the route breakdown" (web `EmptyState`), never a blank panel.
  • Per leg row reproduced field-for-field:
      - index badge  = idx + 1.
      - endpoint     = `leg.from.name || "{lat.toFixed(2)}, {lng.toFixed(2)}"` — empty name falls back
        to the rounded coordinate pair (JS `||`; toFixed = ungrouped, '.'-decimal, locale-independent).
      - Distance     = `convertDistanceFromSI(distance_m, unit).toFixed(1)` + unit (NO grouping — uses
        toFixed, distinct from the grouped Intl path used for energy/currency).
      - Duration     = `Math.round(leg.duration_s)` rendered with the `min` label. THIS IS REPRODUCED
        VERBATIM from the web source (L70): the leg row applies NO seconds->minutes conversion, unlike
        the charge-stop row (L99 `charge_duration_s / 60`). Honesty covenant #5/#9: parity is byte-for-
        byte by mandate, so the magnitude + label match the web exactly on every platform. The quirk is
        documented loudly in Adapter.swift rather than silently "fixed" (which would be drift from spec).
      - Energy       = `formatEnergy(energy_wh, { precision: 1 })` (default kWh -> wh/1000, Intl-grouped,
        non-finite -> "—" per web DEFAULT_EMPTY_DISPLAY).
      - Battery      = `Math.round(start_soc)% -> Math.round(arrival_soc)%`, arrival tinted rose when the
        raw `arrival_soc < 20`, else amber; start emerald (web colors -> design tokens).
  • Charge stop after leg idx (web `idx < chargeStops.length`): blue card with name, `round(s/60)` min,
    soc range, energy, `formatCurrency(cost)` (emerald), + the optional italic "Recommended stop point
    — actual charger locations may vary" note (web `is_recommended`).
  • Hooks bind via facades, not HTTP: useTranslation -> TripLegListStrings (P1/S10); useUnits.formatEnergy
    + useFormatting.formatCurrency/convertDistanceFromSI -> TripLegListUnitMath + the Formatting struct
    (P1/S8 seam). The view never performs I/O.
  • States: loading / empty / error(retry) / stale / offline / content — ALL render (no hidden surfaces).
    The web component is presentational (parent trip-plan query owns load/error); the loading/error/stale/
    offline chrome models that parent lifecycle around the same list, same disposition as sibling 0139.
  • Tailwind -> tokens: emerald->statusSuccess, rose->statusDanger, amber->statusWarning, blue->
    chartSeriesSpeed (web blue-500 == #3b82f6 == chartSeriesSpeed), muted->textMuted, surface->surfaceGlass.
  • a11y: each leg card + each stop card is one combined VoiceOver element reading a full summary;
    decorative glyphs accessibilityHidden; the retry is a labeled Button; FadeIn honors Reduce Motion
    (TSFadeIn); Dynamic Type via tokenized fonts + minimumScaleFactor.
  • Telemetry: view.opened with surface slug "TripLegList" on first start (P1/S11), emitted once.

